# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles must keep LF line endings regardless of
# the developer's platform - they run inside Linux containers, where a
# CRLF shebang line breaks with "bad interpreter: No such file or
# directory". Day 47's backend/docker-entrypoint.sh is the concrete
# reason this exists: this project is developed on Windows, where
# core.autocrlf commonly converts LF to CRLF in the working tree (visible
# throughout this repo's history as git's own "LF will be replaced by
# CRLF" warnings on every commit touching a text file).
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Dockerfile.* text eol=lf
